<p>I apologize for the grammatical errors. English is not my first language. I am not sure if they are simple ones or more complex ones like that involving sentence structure, but I will skim through the SCP and attempt to make fixes. Thank you for pointing that out.</p>
<p>I did not plan on having a humorous effect with the footnotes, and if you could point out in specific which could be construed as such, that would also be appreciated.</p>
<p>You do make a very valid point in that retroactively removing people from the timeline is a significant aftereffect.</p>
<p>It was definitely something that came up while I was working on this SCP, but ultimately, I thought that if utilitarianism was how they quantified how much good they were doing, then exchange of lives would be deemed acceptable by the newer generation.</p>
<p>I know this is a cheesy analogy but if you asked people if they had the power to go back in time and prevent a busfull of people from dying in an accident, chances are a good amount of people would say yes, despite the potential that their actions may ripple out and 'erase' people that would have existed in the future.</p>
<p>As far as the 'Theme' goes, I am not sure what you mean by theme.</p>
<p>Regardless, Thank you very much for the feedback you have provided. I am now a better writer because of it.</p>

