<p>Thank you for your suggestions and compliments. I will look for missing periods. Capitalization and other punctuations, however, are a bit hard for me because English is not my first language. I'll consult a source where the grammatical rules for those can be found&#8230; possibly over the weekend when school isn't deluging me with work. If you are willing, could you point out some of the glaring errors so I can fix them ASAP?</p>
<p>The whole overwrought language thing was a remnant of me trying to make the Silent Crusade out to be some kind of a fanatical organization, but the emphasis of the SCP fell more on the internal schism/ethical dilemma that the Foundation now face. Maybe in the interview log, I can have one of the men speak 'normally' to show that The Silent Crusade picked up members from many different time periods?</p>
<p>I do admit that I was being very verbose in this SCP, but at this point, I recognize the fact that I am not an experienced enough writer to know what exactly I should condense. I am afraid of taking out something that may have been crucial to the story. Do you mind if I do some condensing in sandbox and present it to you for feedback?</p>
<p>Yeah. I think I can take out Protocol Sleeping Nephilim and I can still keep the essence of the Foundation making some other excuses for when SCP-4403-1 going missing is inevitably found out.</p>

