<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>I really like the picture. Like I want it as a wallpaper. Very nice.</li>
<li>It's not&#8230; the <em>worst</em> idea ever. And we <em>are</em> looking for worn-out cliches after all.</li>
<li>The recovered documents thing really saves it, and it's clear you've done a decent bit of history research, or at least know your stuff in general. And the WP links are interesting if you don't already know the details of the event listed.</li>
<li>Ditto the &quot;stapled note&quot; expansion, which is really the meat of the whole thing and raises a few moral questions, as well as exactly what O5-1 is playing at and why&#8230;</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Out of interest, on a scale of 173 to 682, how irrational is my headcanon that the throng of rebelling Foundation staff are actually, ultimately, the group that <em>set up</em> the Silent Crusade (a meaningful name for a hidden faction within another organisation with self-proclaimed higher morals than the rest of it) as a reaction to these events? Or at least end up causing some kind of Stable Time Loop, taking over and re-staffing the Tardis Train (seeing as much of the previous crew would have been killed in the Foundation raid, and who knows how many years they've been doing it according to the machine's internal timeframe?), and ultimately coming back to (maybe a different, altered timeline version of) the Foundation's attention much further down the, ahem, line&#8230;</p>

