<p>I enjoyed reading this, but the main theme of the article bothers me. I mean, if you have an organization dedicated to justice, and that organization has a time machine and weaponry from the future, why not just go back to the very first hunter-gatherer tribes and direct humanity from the beginning? You could instill concepts of justice, empathy, tolerance, and non-violent problem-solving generation after generation as humans spread across the globe. Why limit yourself to just making sure fewer people die in WWII, when you could stop the concept of war?</p>
<p>Of course, this may lead to a world were the Foundation doesn't exist.</p>

